From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XuanTie Linux SDK CI <noreply@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pkg_resources: guard pkgutil.ImpImporter for Python 3.13

pip 22.2.2 vendors a copy of pkg_resources that registers finders and
namespace handlers keyed on pkgutil.ImpImporter at import time. Python
3.12 removed pkgutil.ImpImporter, so on python3 3.13 merely importing
pip._vendor.pkg_resources aborts with:

    AttributeError: module 'pkgutil' has no attribute 'ImpImporter'

pip's importlib metadata backend imports pkg_resources lazily while
scanning egg directories (user_agent() -> get_distribution() ->
find_distributions), so every `pip install` run performed by a recipe
against the native pip (e.g. spdk's python bindings install) crashes.

Guard both registrations with hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'), matching
the fix upstream setuptools/pkg_resources adopted. On Python <= 3.11 the
attribute exists and behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Backport [pypa/setuptools pkg_resources ImpImporter guard]
---
--- a/src/pip/_vendor/pkg_resources/__init__.py
+++ b/src/pip/_vendor/pkg_resources/__init__.py
@@ -2161,7 +2161,8 @@
     return next(dist_groups, ())
 
 
-register_finder(pkgutil.ImpImporter, find_on_path)
+if hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'):
+    register_finder(pkgutil.ImpImporter, find_on_path)
 
 if hasattr(importlib_machinery, 'FileFinder'):
     register_finder(importlib_machinery.FileFinder, find_on_path)
@@ -2312,7 +2313,8 @@
         return subpath
 
 
-register_namespace_handler(pkgutil.ImpImporter, file_ns_handler)
+if hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'):
+    register_namespace_handler(pkgutil.ImpImporter, file_ns_handler)
 register_namespace_handler(zipimport.zipimporter, file_ns_handler)
 
 if hasattr(importlib_machinery, 'FileFinder'):
